    "https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04630": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor (Ladder Rank / In-Residence) Psychiatry Research (JPF04630)",
      "description": "Associate or Full Professor (Ladder Rank / In-Residence) Psychiatry Research (JPF04630) - UC San Diego AP On-Line Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Associate or Full Professor (Ladder Rank / In-Residence) Psychiatry Research (JPF04630) Associate or Full Professor (Ladder Rank / In-Residence) Psychiatry Research Apply now to Associate or Full Professor (Ladder Rank / In-Residence) Psychiatry Research Job #JPF04630 PSYCHIATRY / School of Medicine / UC San Diego Position overview Position title: Psychiatry Research Faculty Salary range: The posted UC Salary scales set the minimum pay at the appointment as determined by appointment type and, if applicable, rank and/or step. The pay range for this position is $120,200 - $255,900. Salary is negotiated annually. Additional compensation may be available if the position includes membership in the Health Sciences Compensation Plan. UC Salary information can be found here: 2026-2027 Academic Salary Scales Application Window Open date: August 31, 2026 Next review date: Sunday, Oct 4, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Tuesday, Aug 31, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Psychiatry within the School of Medicine at UC San Diego is committed to academic excellence within the faculty, staff, and student body. UC San Diego Psychiatry faculty provide exceptional clinical care, cutting-edge research, and educational excellence. As a leader in innovative research, state-of-the-art treatment, and comprehensive education in psychiatry, the Department of Psychiatry is seeking a faculty leader in Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning (AI/ML) and mental health to advance next-generation learning health systems and implementation science. The ideal candidate will bridge clinical psychiatry and data science, leveraging electronic health records (EHR), ML, and real-world data to improve patient outcomes, optimize care delivery, and drive continuous system-level learning. We are seeking a clinical scientist who will translate research into scalable, implemented solutions with measurable impact across behavioral health settings. Responsibilities: Conduct pioneering research in computational psychiatry and mental health. Secure and manage extramural funding to support research initiatives. Publish high-impact findings in leading scientific journals. Mentor and inspire the next generation of AI mental health providers and researchers. Develop and teach advanced courses in psychiatry and related fields (see Education & Training ). Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to identify AI tools and methods to enhance clinical practices and patient care, and may be required to provide clinical services. Engage in community outreach to promote mental health awareness and education. The appointment will be based on the candidate’s background and experience. Series will include 50% Ladder Rank / 50% In-Residence with secured extramural funding or 100% Ladder Rank. A link to the full descriptions of each series is provided for review: Ladder Rank Professor (APM-220) In-Residence Professor (APM-270) As a member of the Health Sciences Compensation Plan, the appointee should be aware that there are limitations on outside professional activities, and clinical moonlighting is expressly prohibited. Additional information can be found here: Health Sciences Compensation Plan (APM-671) Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must have a PhD in clinical mental health science or a related field and/or an MD or equivalent degree. Candidates must have 5+ years of experience in clinical or translational research; an independent, extramurally funded research program (e.g., NIH R01 or similar grants as PI); and 5+ years of research published in high-impact journals, with 25+ publications in psychiatric or related research. Candidates must also have 5+ years of a track record of teaching and/or mentorship activities. Candidates with a PhD who will have clinical duties must have graduated from an APA-accredited doctoral program which includes completion of an APA-accredited internship and have or be eligible for a license from the California Board of Psychology. Candidates with an MD or equivalent degree who will have clinical duties must be board certified or board eligible in their related field and must also be eligible for a California medical license or equivalent certification/permit, as determined by the Medical Board of California. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter COVID-19 Impact Statement -   We understand that the COVID-19 pandemic may have had a substantial impact on academic productivity. In our academic hiring processes, we will be keeping this in mind as we consider achievement relative to opportunity. We encourage you to reflect on constraints on opportunity in your field that were caused by the events of the pandemic and where applicable, to discuss your achievements in this light. (Optional) Misc. / Additional (Optional) Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04630 Help contact: jec182@health.ucsd.edu About UC San Diego The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a university employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, 