    "https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04643": {
      "title": "Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars Search",
      "description": "Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars Search - 2027 (JPF04643) - UC San Diego AP On-Line Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars Search - 2027 (JPF04643) Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars Search - 2027 Apply now to Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars Search - 2027 Job #JPF04643 IGPP / Scripps Institution of Oceanography / UC San Diego Position overview Position title: Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholar Salary range: $75,000/yr with $3,000/yr of discretionary research funds Application Window Open date: September 30, 2026 Next review date: Sunday, Nov 8, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Sunday, Nov 8, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date. Position description The Institute of Geophysics and Planetary Physics (IGPP) at the Scripps Institution of Oceanography, University of California San Diego, has two openings for Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars in any area of geophysics starting in 2027. The PhD awarded to the applicant must have a date no earlier than 3 years before the application deadline, and no later than 6 months after it, though the 3-year limit may be extended up to one year to allow for parental leaves. The appointment cannot start until after the award of the PhD. This is an in-person position with primary work location on the UC San Diego Scripps Institution of Oceanography campus. We seek individuals who show evidence of producing, and continuing to produce, research in geophysics that is of the highest quality. Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars will be 100% supported from the Green Foundation for Earth Sciences. Before submitting an application, applicants should contact potential IGPP mentors to assess their availability to supervise the proposed research project. Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars are encouraged to broaden their experience through interaction with other researchers at IGPP.  Information on recent IGPP research is available at the IGPP Website . Starting salary is $75,000/yr plus benefits, along with $3,000/yr of discretionary research funds. Financial assistance for sponsorship of F-1 STEM OPT and J-1 visas is available. Applications are due by November 8, 2026, and should be submitted online here. Applicants should initiate contact with prospective mentor(s) well before this date. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Must be nearing completion of a PhD program, or have completed a PhD program. Must have research experience in any area of geophysics. Must have experience working in collaboration with other scientists. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Ph.D. in the field of geophysics, or a closely related discipline (for example physics, applied mathematics, engineering). Preferred qualifications N/A Application Requirements Document requirements Dissertation Abstract -   1 page Statement of Research Plans -   Up to 2 pages on standard letter paper 8.5\" x 11\" not including references; 12 pt font size, 1 inch margins on all sides Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. (1-2 pages, 12 point) including a list of publications Reference requirements 2 letters of reference required If referee contact names are provided by deadline, application is noted as complete. There will be one week's grace period to receive letters after the application deadline. In order for reviewers to view all portions of the application, we are requesting that reference writers submit their letters electronically using the link that will be emailed to them once the applicant enters their information on their application. Reference requests are generated automatically by Recruit. Thank you for your assistance in making this electronic review process successful. Apply link: https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04643 Help contact: greenfound@ucsd.edu About UC San Diego The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a university employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California prohibits smoking and tobacco use at all of its university-controlled properties. The UC San Diego Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is available online at: https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf . This report provides crime and fire statistics, as well as institutional policy statements & procedures. Contact the UC San Diego Police Department at (858) 534-4361 if you want to obtain paper copies of this report. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct, are currently being investigated for misconduct, left a position during an investigation for alleged misconduct, or have filed an appeal with a previous employer. Click for more information on Assembly Bill-810 Click for more information on Senate Bill-791 • “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. • UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/4000385/SVSH ] • UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/1001004/Anti-Discrimination ] Job location San Diego, CA Apply now to Cecil H. and Ida M. Green Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars Search - 2027 or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, San Diego is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, San Diego is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports AP On-Line Recruit University of California, San Diego Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04665": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track)Apply nowto Assistant Professor (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) (JPF04665) - UC San Diego AP On-Line Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) (JPF04665) Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) Apply now to Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) Job #JPF04665 CHEMICAL AND NANO ENGINEERING / Jacobs School of Engineering / UC San Diego Position overview Position title: Assistant Professor Salary range: A reasonable salary range estimate for this position is: $107,100-$133,800.\n\nEffective 10/01/2026 A reasonable salary range estimate for this position is: $111,400-$139,200.\n\nThe posted UC Academic salary scales set the minimum pay as determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See UC Salary Scales for this position. The base salary range, from the salary table(s), for this position is: $107,100-$133,800. Effective 10/01/2026 $111,400-$139,200.\n\n“Off-scale salaries” and other components of pay, i.e., a salary that is higher than the published system-wide salary at the designated rank and step, are offered when necessary to meet competitive conditions, qualifications, and experience. ​ ​Additional UCSD salary information can be found on Academic Personnel Services Website Salary Programs and Scales Application Window Open date: September 30, 2026 Next review date: Saturday, Oct 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Monday, May 31, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Chemical and Nano Engineering (CNE) (https://cne.ucsd.edu) ) in the Jacobs School of Engineering at the University of California San Diego invites applications for a tenure- track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. The Department of Chemical and Nano Engineering integrates chemical engineering, nanoengineering, materials science, and emerging technologies to address important challenges in human health, energy, sustainability, and manufacturing. As part of its strategic growth, the Department seeks an outstanding scholar who will establish an innovative and externally funded research program at the intersection of nanosensing, wearable technologies, diagnostics, and healthcare applications. Research Focus: The successful candidate is expected to develop a nationally and internationally recognized research program. Research may span fundamental science, engineering, device development, and translation toward real-world healthcare applications. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: Nanosensors and biosensors for detection and quantitative measurement of biological,\nchemical, or physiological signals; Wearable, flexible, implantable, or minimally invasive sensing technologies for\ncontinuous health monitoring; Point-of-care and decentralized diagnostic technologies for rapid, accessible, and low- cost detection of disease; Micro- and nanoscale devices, microfluidics, lab-on-a-chip systems, and integrated diagnostic platforms; Advanced nanomaterials, biomaterials, and functional materials enabling new sensing and diagnostic capabilities; Bioelectronic and biochemical interfaces that enable high-quality acquisition of\nbiological and physiological data; Multiplexed and multimodal sensing systems that integrate diverse biological, chemical, and physical signals; Data-driven and AI-enabled sensing and diagnostics, including technologies that integrate sensing hardware with advanced data analysis, machine learning, and digital health platforms; and Emerging technologies that enable scalable, affordable, and longitudinal acquisition of health-related data outside traditional clinical settings. Candidates whose research creates connections between fundamental chemical/nanoengineering principles and healthcare technologies are particularly encouraged to apply. Outstanding candidates working in related or emerging areas consistent with the broader strategic goals of the Department will also be considered. Applicants must have earned a Ph.D. in Chemical Engineering, Nanoengineering, Materials Science and Engineering, Bioengineering, or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment. The successful candidate will demonstrate the potential for excellence in scholarship through impactful research, peer-reviewed publications, innovation, and evidence of strong potential for attracting external research support appropriate to career stage. Collaborative Environment: UC San Diego provides an exceptionally collaborative environment for research at the interface of engineering, nanotechnology, medicine, and data science. Depending on research interests, the successful candidate may have opportunities to participate in and collaborate with school-wide and university-wide institutes, centers, and initiatives such as the Institute of Engineering in Medicine, Center for Wearable Sensors, Data Science Institute, Contextual Robotics Institute, Center for Nano-Immunoengineering, and Materials Research Science and Engineering Center, etc. The position also provides opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations across the Jacobs School of Engineering, School of Medicine, Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Herbert Wertheim School of Public Health and Human Longevity Science, and other units across UC San Diego. Teaching and Service: The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the Department's educational mission through effective teaching and mentoring at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching responsibilities may include core and elective courses in Chemical Engineering and/or Nanoengineering, as well as the development of new courses related to the candidate's expertise. Faculty members are also expected to contribute to curriculum development, educational assessment, accreditation activities as appropriate, student mentoring and advising, and departmental, school, university, and professional service. Partner Opportunities: For applicants interested in spousal/partner employment, information about the UC San Diego Dual Career Resources  is available through UC San Diego Academic Personnel (https://academicaffairs.ucsd.edu/aps/partneropp.) Rank and Salary: The appointment will be at the Assistant Professor level. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience and will be based on University of California pay schedules and applicable market conditions. Application: Candidates applying by November 30th will receive full consideration. The position will remain open until filled. Applicants should submit the following materials through UC San Diego Academic Personnel Online Recruit: Cover letter describing the applicant's interest in the position and potential synergies with\nthe Department of Chemical and Nano Engineering and the broader UC San Diego\nresearch community; Curriculum vitae, including publications and professional activities; Research statement describing prior accomplishments, future research plans, and the\nsignificance and potential impact of the proposed research program; Teaching statement describing teaching interests, prior teaching and mentoring\nexperience, and plans for contributing to undergraduate and graduate education; and Names and contact information for three references. About UC San Diego: UC San Diego is committed to creating and maintaining a community in which all individuals are treated with respect and provided opportunities to contribute and succeed. The Department values candidates who will contribute to a collaborative academic environment through excellence in research, education, mentoring, and service. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must have advanced to candidacy or earned their Ph.D. degree in engineering (e.g. Chemical Engineering) or related fields at the time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Applicants must have earned a Ph.D. in Chemical Engineering, Nanoengineering, Materials Science and Engineering, Bioengineering, or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter -   Cover letter describing the applicant's interest in the position and potential synergies with the Department of Chemical and Nano Engineering and the broader UC San Diego research community. Statement of Research -   Research statement describing prior accomplishments, future research plans, and the significance and potential impact of the proposed research program. Statement of Teaching -   Teaching statement describing teaching interests, prior teaching and mentoring experience, and plans for contributing to undergraduate and graduate education; Reference requirements 3-5 letters of reference required Apply link: https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04665 Help contact: m6orozco@ucsd.edu About UC San Diego The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a university employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California prohibits smoking and tobacco use at all of its university-controlled properties. The UC San Diego Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is available online at: https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf . This report provides crime and fire statistics, as well as institutional policy statements & procedures. Contact the UC San Diego Police Department at (858) 534-4361 if you want to obtain paper copies of this report. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct, are currently being investigated for misconduct, left a position during an investigation for alleged misconduct, or have filed an appeal with a previous employer. Click for more information on Assembly Bill-810 Click for more information on Senate Bill-791 • “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. • UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/4000385/SVSH ] • UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/1001004/Anti-Discrimination ] Job location San Diego, CA Apply now to Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, San Diego is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, San Diego is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports AP On-Line Recruit University of California, San Diego Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
