      "description": "Lecturer in Mathematics (JPF04471) - UC San Diego AP On-Line Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Lecturer in Mathematics (JPF04471) Lecturer in Mathematics Apply now to Lecturer in Mathematics Job #JPF04471 MATHEMATICS / Physical Sciences / UC San Diego Position overview Position title: Lecturer Salary range: A reasonable annual salary range estimate for this position is $70,997 - $75,301 The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay at the appointment as determined by appointment type and if applicable, rank and/or step is here https://www.ucop.edu/academic-personnel-programs/_files/2025-26/represented-july-2025-scales/t15.pdf Application Window Open date: March 10, 2026 Most recent review date: Friday, Jun 19, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Mar 10, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Mathematics, within the School of Physical Sciences at UC San Diego, is committed to academic excellence and diversity within the faculty, staff, and student body. The Department is looking for candidates in all areas and specialties of mathematics. The Lecturer will teach depending on the needs of the department. Duties include instruction in courses on topics related to mathematics. The lecturer will likely be teaching a few courses per week and will hold office hours for students. Appointments range from one (1) or more quarters based on departmental needs. Department : https://math.ucsd.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Master's Degree  in Mathematics or a related field and 1 or more years of teaching experience. Preferred qualifications PhD in Mathematics or a related field Experience teaching large classroom sizes (100-300 students) Outstanding Teaching Evaluations Prior University level teaching experience Research experience and a commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion are highly desirable. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Teaching Evaluations -   All of the evaluations of teaching as an instructor or teaching assistant, including comments from students (if available) for the last two years. If not available, submit comments/feedback received from students and/or colleagues Reference requirements 1-4 letters of reference required One recommendation letter specifically addressing teaching  is required for all applicants. Apply link: https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04471 Help contact: apstaff@math.ucsd.edu About UC San Diego The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a university employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California prohibits smoking and tobacco use at all of its university-controlled properties. The UC San Diego Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is available online at: https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf . This report provides crime and fire statistics, as well as institutional policy statements & procedures. Contact the UC San Diego Police Department at (858) 534-4361 if you want to obtain paper copies of this report. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to an